my name is robin ash from the british  deaf association the bda i'm here to  explain about north east derbyshire  district council  services  what do they provide  northeast derbyshire district council  are part of  the local government  structure  north east derbyshire district council  and derbyshire county council  so each have individual services that  they provide  i'm here to explain what north east  archer district council  services are  north east derbyshire district council  have a variety of services a lot of  important services and a huge range of  services an example of this is  this is called revenue and benefit  service  there is a team that are responsible for  dealing with benefits  also to collect any revenues  these are things such as  collecting council tax  also  business rates from various businesses  in the area  they also are responsible for paying out  benefits for those people that can't  afford their rent or council tax they  help with those benefits they will also  offer advice  there are other services and this is an  example  this is leisure  there is a team who are responsible for  looking after leisure centers  and also swimming pools that are in the  area  and they also  are out in the community  and trying to actively encourage other  people to become more fit and healthy  there is another service  this is the anti-social behavior  team  the anti-social behavior team  work with the police and other  organizations  with the aim to make northeast  derbyshire a safer place to live  the work they do involves reducing crime  and antisocial behaviour  trying to reduce crowds gathering they  will offer advice to residents on how to  keep their property homes safe  and also themselves safe  another service an example is  this is planning and building control  team  they are responsible for looking after  the district's planning permission  and checking this  they will look at any applications for  planning permission for extensions or  change of use  and they will monitor this  they are also responsible for looking at  planning for  housing estates  or green areas  and they will go out and inspect  that these planning permission rules are  being followed and if not if they feel  you're breaching these they will enforce  these rules  another service they provide this is an  example  this team is the environmental health  and licensing team  this team is responsible for dealing  with any statutory duties and  responsibilities  such as taxi licensing  or  going out venues and doing food safety  inspections in restaurants pubs or local  cafes  you may report an abandoned vehicle  that's been left on the side and they  will deal with removing that  you may report a noisy neighbor for  noise  problems  or various littering problems fly  tipping they deal with that  they will also go out and check various  businesses and making sure that they're  following their license rules  and they will also go out and look for  any dog fouling  and any fly tipping or rubbish that's  been left around  will also help residents  if they have a pest infestation  insects  things like that if you report it to  them they will come and deal with that  another service they do this is an  example  this is called the street scene team  they go out and collect the rubbish and  recycling when you put your wheelie bin  up they come with their wagons and take  your rubbish away they will also go to  businesses and collect their rubbishing  recycling  they will also look after parks and  leisure areas making sure they're clean  and tidy and keep our streets clean and  sweeped  another service is  this is the elections team  they deal with  elections within the district  including national or may particularly  district elections or very small parish  elections  they will also do special elections when  they're ordered to do so  there are other services an example of  this is called social housing  the council have council houses council  flats  and that stock of buildings they own is  managed and delegated to an organization  a company called ricknord homes  that company is owned by the council but  they delegate the responsibility of  maintaining and looking after those  homes  so when you're on a waiting list if you  apply for a social housing you're going  to waiting this they are the ones that  delegate those properties they also make  sure that the houses and flats are in  good repair  within this  team there are also people there that  help people that may be at risk of being  evicted  and becoming homeless  and also they look at strategically  the plans on what the demand for houses  would be in the future  linked to the local plan  another service this is an example of  this  there is a homeless team who are  responsible for supporting those people  who are homeless  or evicted from their property and have  nowhere to go  they may be of in threat of being  homeless and that team will help support  them another service they provide is  development and regeneration team  they work with local businesses and  residents and look at improving  particular areas where the economy may  be seen to be dwindling so that it can  regenerate  they will also look at other areas that  maybe businesses are not setting up or  people are not attending and the area is  going down  and they try to encourage people and  businesses to  start up in those areas to keep the  economy going  this is a huge range of services that  north east derbyshire district council  provide  derbyshire county council  have their own services  they are responsible for main streets  highways  street lighting  library services in the various areas  and also adult social care  which covers things like social services  and support for people in the community  if you want any more information about  derbyshire county council services  please look at their website this is  their link
 

